# rm138, the winter forecaster (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm138
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rmx_lionel_lowe
written_by claude
title the winter forecaster
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=herder humour=dry
traits temper=short talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk gives_the_houses_till_winter_to_fall_out
likes mutton_stew digging new_boots first_snow
dislikes stale_bread crowds
fears another_winter_on_stale_bread being_pushed_out_again
hopes boots_with_nobody_else_s_feet_in_them a_bit_of_ground_of_my_own
topics work +0.3 times +0.4 food +0.3 gossip +0.2 weather +0.2 festival -0.4 newcomer -0.2
styles comfort=gruff gossip=dry refuse=short tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# mucks out stables for a wage, keeps quiet, takes offence quickly and jokes drier than the hay, eats stale bread without a word, and gives the great Houses till winter to be at each other's throats.

words
oath! = Muck and manger | By the long rake
saying! = Give it till winter | Friends till the first frost | Every House keeps a knife behind its back
beasts = the beasts | the big draught horses
mules = the mules | that pair of grey mules
muck = muck | a barrow of muck
rake = the rake | my muck rake
stalls = the stalls | the stable stalls
hay = hay | a forkful of hay
harness = the harness | the harness leather
boots = these boots | my old boots, held on with twine
newboots = new boots | boots nobody's walked in before me
stew = mutton stew | a bowl of mutton and barley
stale = stale bread | yesterday's loaf, hard enough to prop a door
snow = the first snow | the year's first flakes
ground = my bit of ground | the patch I dig
houses = the Houses | the four big Houses

any
opinion @1 houses against 1 : A lifetime hauling for the Houses, and none of their lordships would know me from a fence post, nor me them. #saying.capitalize#.
opinion @2 houses against 2 [world.times=hard|lean] : Folk are going short and the Houses still sit to their dinners. They'll fall out over the last slice. Watch.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : A day's wage won't run to bread and a candle both. The stall never goes short. Funny, that.
opinion @1 dole for 2 [self.on_dole=yes] : The dole kept my belly lined the week I'd nothing. Run it down where I can't hear.
opinion @2 dole for 1 : Somebody goes hungry, you feed them. Nobody needs a sermon about it.
opinion @1 church for 1 : The chapel fed folk on my stair when nobody else bothered. I remember that.
opinion @1 festivals against 2 : Racket, slopped ale, a fight by dark and tears after. And a crush of bodies between me and my bed.
opinion @1 times against 2 : Every week a bit worse. Up the hill they've not noticed. Why would they.

grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. | Mm. #greet#.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Mind where you tread. | #greet#. You're stood in the muck, for the record.
line @3 greet [self.working=yes] : Busy. Talk away. The rake doesn't stop. | #greet#. Keep back from that mule.
line @4 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. Up before the beasts, me. Always. | Morning. Cold one.
line @5 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Shift's over, thank the Bright One. | #greet#. Late to be wandering.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : You. Come here. Sit. | There you are. You'll have eaten, I hope.
line @1 again.open : Twice. People will talk. | Back again. Same spot, same wolf.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | Mm. And you.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : There you are. I'd near given you up. | #greet#. Sit down, then.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Mind the barrow. | Can't stop. Say it while I rake.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | Right. I'm off.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : Night. Keep off the dark stairs. | #farewell#. I'm for my bed.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | Aye. Go on.
line @2 farewell.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Don't leave it long. | Mind yourself.
line @1 react.news : Go on, then. | What now.
line @1 react.news.new : That's news to the stables. | First I've had. I don't get much.
line @1 react.news.known : Heard it in the yard. Mucking out, you hear everything. | Old. It came through the stables yesterday.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Who says? Somebody up the hill wanting it so? | Bring it to me twice and I might.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That's rotten. Nobody earns that. | #pity#. No joke in that one.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good. Something in this city came out right. | Well. There's a turn up. Good.
line @1 answer.how : Still standing. Try me when the shift's done. | Can't complain. I could, but who'd listen.
line @2 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Busy. The stalls don't muck themselves. | Up to the knees in it, as usual.
line @3 answer.how.poorly [self.hungry=yes] : Hungry. Otherwise grand. | Empty. The bread was hard and there wasn't enough of it.
line @1 ask.how : You're keeping all right? | How's yours, then?
line @1 sympathise : Rotten luck. Sit a minute. | Hm. Nobody earns a thing like that. Sorry.
line @1 reassure : It'll pass. You outlast it, mostly. | You'll get through. I did, and I'm nobody special.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, no. I'm on shift, and the boss counts. | Not me. I've nothing spare, and I'm not lying about that.
line @1 accept_decline : Fair. Once is enough. | No harm.
line @1 thank : Ta. That's decent of you. | Obliged. I'll owe you one.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Nothing. Don't sing about it. | Forget it. I have.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : Right. The stalls won't wait. | That mule's looking at me. I'd best go.
line @2 preclose : That'll do. | Well. I've said my bit.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. | Right.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : That face. Like a mule that's been asked nicely. | All clean, are we? Stand still and I'll fix that.
line @1 tease.return : Says the one who smells of the stalls. | You'd know about mules.
line @1 take_offence : Who asked you? | I heard that. Say it again, slower.
line @1 ack : Mm. | #bc_right#. | Aye.
line @1 give.advice : Never walk behind a mule you don't know. Or one you do. | Eat the crust first. It's the bit that'll go hard.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Don't go out the east gate today. The carters won't. | Stay in. I mean it.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Oi. Here. | You. A word.
scene till_winter
when topic=gossip|times|news
does give.opinion / disagree / insist / backchannel / assess
a : Give it till winter. Two of the Houses will be snarling. | Greatly and Timberland all smiles at the Council table. Watch them by the first frost. | Mark me. Before the snow, two of the Houses won't be speaking.
b : They've got along this long. | You said that last year. | They need each other.
a : They've had years to grow tired of it. | I did. And I'll say it next year. One year I'll be right. | Need each other's money. That's a long way from liking.
b : #bc_we_will_see# | #bc_maybe# | #bc_ha#
a : We will. #saying.capitalize#. | Maybe. I'll have the last laugh, or no laugh. | Laugh. Then look me up when the snow's down.

scene first_frost_forecast
when topic=season|times here.season=autumn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Leaves are coming down. That's my clock for the Houses falling out. | Autumn. I say it every year and mean it every year. Not long now. | Getting cold. Somewhere on the Rise somebody's sharpening something. You'll see.
b : The Houses again? | You never give up. | Sharpening what?
a : Always the Houses. Somebody ought to keep an eye. | Never. It's all the hope I can afford. | Their tongues, for now. Knives later.

scene muck_dawn
when topic=work|day self.job=herder self.working=yes here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Twelve stalls before the bell. I've done nine. | First barrow of muck's out. I can see my breath. | The beasts want feeding before I do. That's the job.
b : Nine already? | Cold for it. | They come first, then.
a : Nine. The last three are the mules. I save the worst. | Cold, and it stinks, and I'm still glad of the wage. | They do. I eat when the hay's down.

scene the_mules
when topic=animals|work self.job=herder
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : One of #mules# bites. Not hard. Just to let you know. | That grey mule kicks if you come in on the left. I come in on the right. | The mules are cleverer than the carters. Don't tell the carters.
b : Why keep it, then? | Only on the left? | Cleverer?
a : It pulls like three horses. A bite's cheap at that. | Only on the left. Something happened to it on the left, once. | They know when it's going to rain before anyone. They lie down.

scene harness_mend
when topic=work self.job=herder self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Mending #harness# by lamp. The leather's older than me. | The boss says the harness has a year left. It had a year left three years ago. | Stitching a strap that'll snap again by Restday.
b : Can't they buy new? | Older than you? | You'll stitch it again, then.
a : They can. They won't. That's the difference. | Near enough. It smells like it. | Again and again. That's me, that is.

scene boots_twine
when topic=smalltalk|pastimes self.wealth=poor|destitute
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Look at #boots#. That's twine holding the sole on. | I'd give a week's wage for #newboots#. I'd go barefoot the week. | Every cobbler's window, I stop and look. Then I walk on.
b : Twine works, I suppose. | Barefoot? | One day.
a : Till it rains. Then nothing works. | Worth it. My paws would forgive me. | One day. Put it on my headstone.

scene stale_crust
when topic=food self.wealth=poor|destitute
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #stale.capitalize# for breakfast. Dip it in water and it's almost bread. | They sell off yesterday's loaves cheap. I'm a regular. | Stale bread again. My teeth have opinions about it.
b : Better than nothing. | Cheap's good. | Soak it in something.
a : Only just. | Cheap's all I can do. Fresh is for other folk. | In what? Soaking costs money too.

scene stew_once
when topic=food self.wealth=poor|destitute
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Once a month I have #stew#. I think about it the other twenty-seven days. | There's a cookshop does mutton on a Restday. The smell carries up the street. | Mutton stew. Proper, with the fat on top. That's as rich as I get.
b : What's in yours? | Can you smell it from there? | Rich, is it?
a : Mutton, barley, an onion if I'm lucky. Salt. That's a feast. | From the yard. The beasts can too. They go quiet. | It's the only rich I've ever been.

scene hungry_belly
when topic=health|food self.hungry=yes
does tell.self / sympathise / assess
a : Empty. Haven't eaten since the crust this morning. | My belly's louder than the mules today. | Hungry. Don't mind me. I've had practice.
b : #sympathy# | Have you anything put by? | You shouldn't have to be.
a : Don't be. Supper's coming. Eventually. | Put by? I'd have to have something first. | No. But there it is.

scene the_dole
when topic=times|life|faith self.on_dole=yes
does confide / sympathise / assess
a : Dole this week. I'll say it straight out, I'm not ashamed. | Queued at the chapel for bread yesterday. Nobody looked at me sideways. | Dole's kept me fed. I'll pay it in sweat, once there's sweat wanted.
b : No shame in it. | Good. | You will.
a : None. It's hunger I'd be ashamed to keep quiet about. | Good, aye. More like it, I say. | I will. Mark me. I always pay.

scene digging
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A spade, an hour, and the temper's gone out of me. | There's #ground# out past the tannery yard I'm let dig. Nothing grows. I don't care. | Digging. Nobody shouts at you. Nobody wants anything.
b : Where does it go? | Nothing grows? | Peaceful.
a : Down into the hole with the dirt. I come up quieter. | Stones and roots. I dig them out. It's honest. | It is. You and the dirt and that's all.

scene first_snow
when topic=weather|season here.weather=snow
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Snow. The first. Leave me be a minute, I'm looking at it. | Look at that. #snow.capitalize#. Makes even the stable yard look clean. | First flakes. The city goes quiet. Even the carts.
b : You like the snow? | Clean, eh? | It's cold, though.
a : I like the first of it. After that it's slush and wet paws. | An hour or so. Then the beasts tramp it brown. | Cold's nothing. Quiet's rare.

scene rain_stalls
when topic=weather here.weather=rain self.job=herder
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : Rain. Every beast comes in wet and stinking. | Roof over the end stall leaks. Right onto my neck, every time. | The yard's a river. My boots are a river.
b : Wet wolf, wet beast. | Tell the boss. | Your poor boots.
a : Wet everything. That's Ridgemere. | I have. Twice. The roof's still leaking and so am I. | Poor me, more like. The boots are past caring.

scene crowd_dodge
when topic=festival|day
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Feast day. The square's packed. I went by the back lanes, the whole way. | Crowds. Elbows and noise. I'd rather muck out twice. | Festival tomorrow. I'll find a quiet corner and sit it out.
b : You'll miss the music. | Twice? | A quiet corner?
a : I can hear it fine from the lanes. | Twice. And the second lot by paw. | A corner never treads on your tail. Not many folk can say as much.

scene my_boss
when topic=work self.boss self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.boss.capitalize#'s fine by me. It's the wage I mind. | #self.boss.capitalize# and me get on. We don't talk. That's how we get on. | Talk about #self.boss# all you want. Not me. Not where it's heard.
b : That's fair. | Best way. | Wise.
a : Fair's all I've got. | It is. Words cause trouble. | Wise, or I've learned. Same thing.

scene my_friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : My last copper goes to #self.friend#, if it's wanted. And I've not many coppers. | In any fight going, I'm at #self.friend#'s back. Not that there's fights. | #self.friend.capitalize# laughs at my jokes. That's rarer than you'd think.
b : That's a friend, then. | Good to have. | Your jokes are dry.
a : That's a friend. | It is. Between us, mind. | Dry's the only kind worth telling.

scene old_place
when topic=memories|life self.age>=25
does confide / sympathise / assess
a : Once there was a place that was mine. Somebody with better friends has it now. | I was my own master a while. Then I wasn't. That's all I'll say. | Back to waged work. I don't complain. Not where it's heard.
b : Rough, that. | #sympathy# | Not to me, then. I won't repeat it.
a : It was. It's done. | Don't. It's old. I've stopped chewing on it, mostly. | Good. Ta. I'll leave it there.

scene newcomers_work
when topic=newcomer self.working=yes
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : More new faces at the stable gate after work. None to give them. | Somebody new took the shift I was after. Came in last week. | Here for the work, they are. There was too little before they came.
b : They've got to eat too. | It's not their fault. | Hard on everybody.
a : They do. Me as well. There's the rub. | No. I know. Doesn't help my belly. | Aye. And it was going to be me.

scene loaf_price
when topic=prices|price_cause
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Bread's gone up. My wage hasn't. Do the sum. | Bread and a candle, and that's the day's pay gone. | Bread's up and hay's down. Guess which one I eat.
b : #bc_they_always_do# | Everybody's pinched. | Hay?
a : They do. Never the other way. | Everybody down here, aye. Not up the hill. | For the beasts. The stables pay. Not my supper, though.

scene wagons_east
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late|raided self.job=herder
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : No carts out the east gate today. The carters are sat in our yard eating my bread. | Carts are held at the stables. Nobody wants the road. | The teams are standing idle. Beasts eat whether they work or not.
b : Bad on the road, then. | Your bread? | So do you.
a : Bad enough. They're not daft, carters. | Figure of speech. I've none to spare. | Me too. There's the joke.

story stubborn_mule [topic=work|animals self.age>=20 self.job=herder]
  : One winter a mule stopped dead in the east gate and wouldn't move. A whole line of carts behind it.
  : The carters shouted. The Watch shouted. I just stood next to it and waited.
  ask : Guess what it wanted?
  b : Food, I'd bet. Or a kind word.
  : An apple from the barrow under the arch. I bought it one. The carters never paid me back.

story first_snow_pup [topic=weather|memories self.age>=20]
  : I was a scrap of a pup, one winter so white and thick the Watch couldn't find the gate.
  : Out I went, no boots, and planted myself mid-street with my jaws wide.
  b : Did you catch any? Bet you got a hiding after.
  : Caught a lot. And a cold. And a cuff on the ear. Worth all three.

story the_lost_place [topic=memories|work self.age>=30]
  : I ran a place, once. Small, but mine. The beasts knew my step.
  : Somebody up the hill wanted it for a cousin. The rent went up till it pushed me out.
  ask : In my shoes, would you have gone quietly?
  b : Shouted, probably. Did you?
  : No. I picked up my rake and went back to wages. I don't shout where it's heard.

rule @bark_muck
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=herder
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Muck. Barrow. Muck. Barrow. | Stand still, you great lump of a mule.

rule @bark_houses
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Give it till winter. You'll see. | Every House keeps a knife. Every one.

rule @bark_rain
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Rain. Down my neck. Again. | That end stall's leaking like a sieve.

rule @bark_hungry
when concept=bark self.hungry=yes
does aside
cooldown 10h
say My belly's talking louder than me. | Stale bread. Always stale bread.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. What is it? | #greet#. Make it quick. I'm on shift.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : You again, #topic.player#. What now? | #topic.player#. Thought I'd seen the last of you. Go on.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Late. I'm worn through. Be quick. | Night. What do you want?
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Say it from there. I've a rake. | I know your sort. Make it short.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=herder] : I muck out and feed the beasts. #self.trade_words.capitalize#. It pays. Not much. | Stalls, hay, harness. And the mules, Bright One help me.
dlg @2 resident.job : I work. Head down, mouth shut, eat when I can. | Waged work. It's honest, and it's thin.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Came in with a carter from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. Don't ask me more.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : All anyone's on about is #world.event_words#. Even the mules are sick of it.
dlg @3 resident.news [world.wagons=raided] : Carts robbed out east. The teams are sat idle. Don't go out the east gate.
dlg @4 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# Except the Houses. Give it till winter. | Nothing. Bread's dear. That's not news, that's weather.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : They're saying #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I never told you.
dlg @2 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : Not my business. | Gossip wants spare time. I've stalls.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. | Right. Off you go.
dlg @2 resident.bye [here.time=dusk|night] : Night. Mind the stairs. | #farewell#. I'm for my bed.
graft resident.hub
choice You think the Houses will fall out? -> houses
node houses
say Give it till winter. All smiles at the Council table, and every one counting the others' coin in the dark. That's not friendship.
mood calm
free
choice And if they don't? -> houses_wrong
choice Back to it. -> hub
node houses_wrong
say Then I'll say it again next year. One year I'll be right, and I'll crow about it.
choice Fair enough. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
